 "_about": "Letter grids of the four Enochian Watchtowers. rows[0] is the top row; each row is a 12-letter string, index 0 = leftmost square. U/V are one letter in Dee's alphabet (as are I/Y); grids keep the source spelling.",
 "goldenDawn": {
  "_about": "Golden Dawn working version. The GD tablets come from the 1587 Tabula Recensa (Raphael's reformed table), but GD manuscripts (Book H, Westcott's abridgement of Sloane MS 307) print several squares with 2-3 letters. This set gives ONE primary letter per square: the Recensa letter as transcribed by J. H. Peterson, except Air row 12 col 1 (see cellNotes). cellNotes lists every other letter seen in GD-lineage sources (Crowley Plate III, GD Book H) and in the 1584 table. Regardie's printed GD plates could not be consulted (in copyright, not online), so this is not a facsimile of them.",
